[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2427684483","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98392#issuecomment-2427684483","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98392","id":2427684483,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Qs4aD","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-21T20:45:20Z","updated_at":"2024-10-21T20:45:20Z","body":"I needed to say goodbye to lvalue references. Besides the rather explicit crashes on conversions, the explicit lvalue conversions were being used automatically leading to unit test crashes already.\r\n\r\nPointers make somewhat more sense anyway because it can be nullable, which is fitting in this case, requiring no explicit crash.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2427684483/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2428970363","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98392#issuecomment-2428970363","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98392","id":2428970363,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6QxyV7","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-22T11:00:29Z","updated_at":"2024-10-22T11:09:58Z","body":"Ok, I refactored to use `variant.get_xxx` notation instead. This is closer to `std::get<XXX>(variant)` syntax, with the main difference being that we return a pointer rather than an lvalue reference, which is null on type failure rather than crashing.\r\n\r\nI also added getters for all the other types, except Object which already has such a getter (`get_validated_object()`). This will allow in-place modification and non-copy use of all held types. Keep in mind this is not _new_ behavior: Variant can already be modified in-place with `call`. The main addition in this PR is to allow the modification to be typesafe.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2428970363/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2445337596","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98392#issuecomment-2445337596","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98392","id":2445337596,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6RwOP8","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-29T21:10:39Z","updated_at":"2024-10-29T21:10:39Z","body":"These functions seem basically the same as the `VariantInternal::get_*()` functions.\r\n\r\nGiven that we want to expose something like this on the GDExtension side, I'm not sure what the API _should_ be. We could certainly make matching `VariantInternal::get_*()` functions in godot-cpp, so long as Godot provided us with a way to get the underlying pointers, although, perhaps that isn't the friendliest API?\r\n\r\nSo, probably the first thing is we need to decide on what API we want within Godot, and then we can figure out how to make the same work in GDExtension and godot-cpp.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2445337596/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2470970794","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98392#issuecomment-2470970794","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98392","id":2470970794,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TSAWq","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-12T16:20:07Z","updated_at":"2024-11-12T16:20:20Z","body":"> These functions seem basically the same as the `VariantInternal::get_*()` functions.\r\n\r\nOh, I had no idea those existed! There remains a small difference in that my implementation checks for variant state first. This may or may not be wanted; the `std::get<>()` API crashes when it's in a wrong state, and most uses of this API would probably also not check for null before de-referencing. I'm not sure what I prefer.\r\n\r\n> Given that we want to expose something like this on the GDExtension side, I'm not sure what the API _should_ be. We could certainly make matching `VariantInternal::get_*()` functions in godot-cpp, so long as Godot provided us with a way to get the underlying pointers, although, perhaps that isn't the friendliest API?\r\n\r\nThis would be blocked by Variant not exposing `PackedArrayRef`, a change proposed in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98373 but not accepted (or sufficiently discussed) yet.\r\n \r\n> So, probably the first thing is we need to decide on what API we want within Godot, and then we can figure out how to make the same work in GDExtension and godot-cpp.\r\n\r\nThere seem to be a few scattered uses of the ``*VariantInternal::get_xxx(variant)`` API in some spots, but mostly `*VariantGetInternalPtr<xxx>::get_ptr(variant)` seems to be used (which uses the above internally). That's probably because a lot of the code using it is using templates, and using this code to abstract its logic.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2470970794/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2481174751","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98392#issuecomment-2481174751","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98392","id":2481174751,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6T47jf","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-17T10:52:19Z","updated_at":"2024-11-17T10:52:19Z","body":"Superseded by #99201 because Variant internal has the proposed functionality already, an equivalent  just needs to be exposed to gdextension.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2481174751/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]